Not sure I follow. You can use them in a template function like this:

``` javascript
{
  templates: {
    item: (data) => {
      return `My name is ${data.name}`;
    }
}
```

True! You can use them in a function.

But they can't be used as values. They are very much hardcoded inside the function that use them. You can't do:

``` js
var myTemplate = `bar ${foo}`;
// already translated as a string using the context

var myRenderedTemplate = fn(`baz ${bar}`);
// Translated to string before the function call
```
